    struct vub300_mmc_host *vub300 = kref_to_vub300_mmc_host(kref);
    struct mmc_host *mmc = vub300->mmc;
    ...
    mmc_free_host(mmc);
}
...
err_free_host:
    mmc_free_host(mmc);
```
Reason:
The fix replaces `devm_mmc_alloc_host()` with `mmc_alloc_host()` for non-managed allocation, so the `mmc_host` is no longer automatically freed when the device is removed. Instead, the memory is explicitly freed in the kref callback `vub300_delete` (via `mmc_free_host(mmc)`), ensuring that the host structure remains valid until the last reference is released. Additionally, a new error label `err_free_host` is added to properly free the host on probe failure paths, preventing memory leaks.

